WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.127
The print function gives us a quick way to see what the program is doing.

00:00:06.127 --> 00:00:09.387
Here we store a name, age, sales, and costs.

00:00:09.387 --> 00:00:15.312
The print statements combine labels with values so the output has context.

00:00:15.312 --> 00:00:22.897
The last line calculates sales minus costs directly, so with one thousand in sales and eight hundred in costs,

00:00:22.897 --> 00:00:25.002
the displayed profit is two hundred.

00:00:25.545 --> 00:00:30.762
Print is simple, but it is extremely useful while learning and debugging.

00:00:30.762 --> 00:00:37.747
If you are unsure what a variable contains at a certain point, printing it is often the fastest way to inspect the

00:00:37.747 --> 00:00:39.095
program state.
